<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#horse-trade">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horse trade</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as horses from North Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The horse trade refers to the exchange of horses, often over long distances, for military and prestige purposes. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-sudan">central Sudan</a>, horses imported from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> were vital to cavalry warfare. The Kanem-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a> built its military power partly on such imported horses, often exchanged for enslaved captives.</p></div>
